---
// The side marker for a case-study header: which half of the practice this project sat on,
// and — since chooser andrewshiau-panel-marks Q5/06 — the way back to the index.
//
// The panel head used to open with the logo and then this line, so the figure was drawn
// TWICE, stacked, ~30px apart, at two sizes. The logo was there to be the link home; this
// line was there to name the side. One of them had to go, and the marker is the one that
// carries a fact, so it took the link as well.
//
// It draws the LOGO's figure, not the flat 22×8 glyph the index uses, and it is side-aware
// (MarkFigure.astro): the diagonal pair where the page sat on both halves of the practice, a
// single dot in the one hue where it sat on one. A pairing is only drawn where there is one —
// the diagonal's whole subject is two things joined, and on `/work/luthier/` there is no
// second thing for the rule to reach.
//
// The WORD stays here, visible. The index hides it now (Q1/05) because eight rows repeating
// "Design + Build" was the loudest thing in that column; a panel head prints one marker, so
// the word costs nothing and it is what keeps the marker legible in greyscale — navy and olive
// are 2.14:1 apart (STYLE.md). SideDot is not used because its glyph is the flat one built for
// a meta line's baseline; only the geometry differs, and both read their side from the same
// `sideOf`, so the fact still can't drift from the index.
import { sideOf, SIDE_LABEL } from '../data/experiments';
import MarkFigure from './MarkFigure.astro';
interface Props { href: string }
const { href } = Astro.props;
const side = sideOf(href);
---
<p class="smark">
  <a class="smark-home" href="/" aria-label="andrewshiau — home"
    ><MarkFigure side={side} />{SIDE_LABEL[side]}</a
  >
</p>
